# The model the whisper server loads.
#
# The name matters: the server reads its settings through
# pydantic-settings with env_nested_delimiter "__", so the section is
# WHISPER and the field is MODEL -- the variable is WHISPER__MODEL,
# not WHISPER_MODEL. The old name was read by nobody, which is how a
# compose file could claim one model while the server ran another
# (measured on the production host, 2026-10-28).
#
# The compose file sets the model inline, so this file only matters
# when the service is run by hand. The value below is the one the
# production deployment actually loads: Systran/faster-whisper-small,
# the image default.
#
# Heavier options, if the host ever has the room:
#   Systran/faster-distil-whisper-large-v3   -- fast, accurate, ~1.5GB
#   Systran/faster-whisper-large-v3          -- bigger, more accurate
#   Systran/faster-whisper-medium.en         -- English-only, very small
#   Systran/faster-whisper-small.en          -- tiny, English-only
WHISPER__MODEL=Systran/faster-whisper-small
